[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3983743693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116925#issuecomment-3983743693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116925","id":3983743693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tcxrN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T11:16:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:52:48Z","body":"Not sure what exactly is going on here, and profilers like this can be hard to evaluate and inaccurate, but it's important to note that RID owner has a standard chunk size of 64k to improve performance, so allocating a single RID entry will take up that much for that case, it also adds some overhead for free chunk tracking, so that means 64k plus 64k divided by the size of the item (in this case 8 bytes, as we store a pointer) times 4 bytes, total of that should be 96k unless my math is off\n\nAdd to that, depending on how this is counted, the other data in each RTL, plus other overhead, like how RTL adds an internal scroll bar and timer, hard to tell what comes from where\n\nSo it's pretty difficult to evaluate the exact expected memory cost here and what is reasonable\n\nEdit: It actually allocates a total of `(65536/8)*(16+4)` bytes, which in this case is around 163 KB, it allocates a `Chunk` for each entry (which is the data stored, plus a 32 bit validator, which comes to 16 bytes due to alignment), plus a 32 bit free chunk marker. The number of entries is based on the target chunk size, divided by the size of each entry (in this case 8 bytes, a 64 bit pointer)\n\nSo we're still missing a few KB, as the size for each RTL in your case is around 175 KB, so we're out by about 12 KB","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3983743693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984323314","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116925#issuecomment-3984323314","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116925","id":3984323314,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7te_Ly","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T13:14:04Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T13:14:04Z","body":"> Edit: It actually allocates a total of `(65536/8)*(16+4)` bytes, which in this case is around 163 KB, it allocates a `Chunk` for each entry (which is the data stored, plus a 32 bit validator, which comes to 16 bytes due to alignment), plus a 32 bit free chunk marker. The number of entries is based on the target chunk size, divided by the size of each entry (in this case 8 bytes, a 64 bit pointer)\n\nThis still sounds quite exaggerated. Without enabling the bbcode feature, simply instantiating this class requires allocating 163 KB of memory, far exceeding other components.  \n\nIn my project, there is a list displaying the player's local mods. The `item` in the list uses a custom scene, with each `item` containing two `RichTextLabel` controls (bbcode is not enabled; it is used only because `Label` does not support text selection) and numerous other UI controls (`Label`, `Panel`, `Button`, etc.). In my test, 129 mods were loaded, but almost no memory usage from other controls was found in the profiling software. Only the constructor of `RichTextLabel` occupied `41.7 MB`, with `items.make_rid` alone accounting for `39 MB`. Is there room for optimization here?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984323314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984353153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116925#issuecomment-3984353153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116925","id":3984353153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tfGeB","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T13:19:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T13:19:48Z","body":"It would be possible to reduce the allocation chunk size for the RID owner probably for this specific case, but I'd say that RTL shouldn't necessarily be expected to be cheap\n\nNote that it stays at 163 KB for a long time, and will relatively soon become a smaller part of the memory than all the data inside the RTL itself I'd say\n\nBut we should evaluate if it'd be good to shrink the allocation size of the RID owner here to reduce the baseline, though that would have to be done carefully and tested for performance as it'd have consequences for large data cases","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3984353153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4004372399","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116925#issuecomment-4004372399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116925","id":4004372399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7urd-v","user":{"login":"scgm0","id":52148221,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTQ4MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52148221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0","html_url":"https://github.com/scgm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/scgm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T11:26:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T11:26:37Z","body":"> It would be possible to reduce the allocation chunk size for the RID owner probably for this specific case, but I'd say that RTL shouldn't necessarily be expected to be cheap\n\nIs it only `RichTextLabel` that uses RID owner? I haven't seen such a large memory footprint from RID owners elsewhere in the heap analysis (in my project, it accounts for over 20% of the memory peak).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4004372399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/40